{"tool_name":"yacrd","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"yacrd","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa262"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Yet Another Chimeric Read Detector, with long-read mapper result as input.","home_url":"https://github.com/natir/yacrd","keywords":["High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Sequence Analysis, DNA"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4},"biotools":{"id":"yacrd","home":"https://github.com/natir/yacrd","license":"MIT","summary":"upstream tools for long-read genome assembly.\n\nLong Read mapping tools provides all match they found in read dataset, for many usage some of match aren't usfull, this programme provide some filter to remove it. This soft can be replace by a simple script in awk, bash, python.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T08:44:30Z","last_update_date":"2021-03-18T11:47:54Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:yacrd","credit":[{"email":"pierre.marijon@inria.fr","name":"Pierre Marijon","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Chimera detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0450"},{"term":"Pairwise sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"yacrd","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAA262","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s) 2020. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved. For permissions, please e-mail: journals.permissions@oup.com.Motivation: Genome assembly is increasingly performed on long, uncorrected reads. Assembly quality may be degraded due to unfiltered chimeric reads; also, the storage of all read overlaps can take up to terabytes of disk space. Results: We introduce two tools: yacrd for chimera removal and read scrubbing, and fpa for filtering out